Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:16:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Word 4-gram + grapheme 8-gram decoding for B: grid, results,
 bucket upload

- lm_decode B --lm-kind dual, grid on all 2,000 dev2k: alpha 0.2, beta 1.0,
  g_alpha 0.3, g_beta 1.0 (edge extension _dual2 confirms the same point)
- v6 test WER / WER_seg / CER / GER 14.59 / 7.90 / 3.23 / 4.10
  (B + grapheme 8-gram 14.26 / 8.05 / 3.20 / 4.06, A 14.72 / 8.95 / 3.68 / 4.61)
- spacing-only errors 3,441 -> 3,018, word errors 9,268 -> 8,714, but inserted
  words 1,474 -> 2,280, so WER is worse than the grapheme LM alone
- upload_hf_bucket.py --what dual: *_dual* eval files to the private bucket
- result files in reference/grapheme/, write-up and budget in NOTES.md

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
